1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
cdfc — Every checker tells you what it found.

2
00:00:03,660 --> 00:00:07,860
One control. No strict mode, no sheet selector, no skip-empty-rows box.

3
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:13,260
Every setting here would change what gets checked — without changing what the report says was checked.

4
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:20,000
The declaration. Two numbers, the same size, the same weight, the same ink.

5
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:25,400
The moment one is bigger, the reader has been told which matters — and it would be the one nobody checked.

6
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:30,960
The coverage band never fills. The two hatched terms carry no digit, because neither has been measured.

7
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:37,720
Is 3,747 the whole form? No — and a denominator that will not say what it excluded is a coverage lie.

8
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:46,100
505 cells the template computes. 2,505 a filer cannot write. 3,747 left, and that is the denominator.

9
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:51,560
This page is the product. It is not an appendix and it does not live behind a tab.

10
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:58,520
422 cells have a check that the kill gate refused. 1,427 have no candidate at all. Different gaps.

11
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:04,680
Each group carries its own remedy naming the gate that would move it. There is no fallback string.

12
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:11,980
348 candidate checks refused, every row carrying the number that refused it.

13
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:17,940
A rejection without the number that decided it is an opinion with a gate name on it.

14
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:25,040
Gate order. Everything survives G0, G1 and G3-proof. Everything dies at G2, the kill gate.

15
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:31,600
The last two stages say NOT RUN — not "passed everyone". A gate that never ran decided nothing.

16
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:39,300
29 predicates produced the settled count. 0 are admitted through the five gates.

17
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:45,260
Disjoint populations — so the screen says so, rather than leaving a reader to assume.

18
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:52,360
A coverage number that can only rise is a marketing chart. This one fell.

19
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:58,920
1,898 to 1,862 after a template change, and the cause travels with the fall.

20
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:06,620
Nine predicates stopped settling. They did not stop running — detection was not lost.

21
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:15,600
Five seeded defects. All five detected — but only one surfaces as a finding.

22
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:20,800
What it does not claim — It does not read the regulation — 0 of 348 predicates implement a statutory clause.

23
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:25,000
It tells you what it did not check. — This states what was checked and what was not.
